 </h2>
 <div class="UnitReadme-content" data-test-id="Unit-readmeContent">
 <div class="Overview-readmeContent js-readmeContent"><h3 class="h1" id="readme-httpx-package">HTTPX Package</h3>
<p><a href="https://goreportcard.com/report/github.com/chi07/httpx" rel="nofollow"><img src="https://goreportcard.com/badge/github.com/chi07/httpx?v=1" alt="Go Report Card"/></a>
<a href="https://codecov.io/gh/chi07/httpx" rel="nofollow"><img src="https://codecov.io/gh/chi07/httpx/branch/main/graph/badge.svg" alt="codecov"/></a>
<a href="https://github.com/chi07/httpx/actions/workflows/ci.yml" rel="nofollow"><img src="https://github.com/chi07/httpx/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg" alt="CI"/></a></p>
<p>httpx is a lightweight, high-performance HTTP client wrapper for Go, built on top of Resty.
It provides consistent error handling, context-based timeouts, low-allocation JSON decoding, and typed responses via Go generics.</p>
<p>✨ Features</p>
<ul>
<li>🔹 Simple, strongly typed API: Result[T] with Data or Err</li>
<li>🔹 Unified error structure (Error{Code, Message, Fields, Raw})</li>
<li>🔹 Context-based per-request timeout (no leaks)</li>
<li>🔹 Minimal memory allocations (uses []byte directly)</li>
<li>🔹 Built-in retry logic and JSON decoding</li>
<li>🔹 Optional bearer token forwarding</li>
<li>🔹 Fully concurrent and safe for production</li>
</ul>
<p>📦 Installation</p>
<pre><code>go get github.com/chi07/httpx
</code></pre>
<p>🚀 Usage</p>
<p>Basic Example</p>
<pre><code>package main
import (
 &#34;context&#34;
 &#34;fmt&#34;
 &#34;net/http&#34;
 &#34;time&#34;
 &#34;github.com/chi07/httpx&#34;
)
type User struct {
 ID int `json:&#34;id&#34;`
 Name string `json:&#34;name&#34;`
}
func main() {
 client := httpx.New()
 req := httpx.Request{
 URL: &#34;https://api.example.com/users/1&#34;,
 Method: http.MethodGet,
 Timeout: 3 * time.Second,
 }
 res := httpx.Do[User](context.Background(), client, req)
 if res.Err != nil {
 fmt.Println(&#34;Request failed:&#34;, res.Err.Message)
 return
 }
 fmt.Printf(&#34;User: %+v\n&#34;, *res.Data)
}
</code></pre>
<h3 class="h1" id="readme-with-query-headers-and-bearer-token">With Query, Headers, and Bearer Token</h3>
<pre><code>req := httpx.Request{
 URL: &#34;https://api.example.com/search&#34;,
 Method: http.MethodGet,
 QueryParams: map[string]string{
 &#34;q&#34;: &#34;golang&#34;,
 },
 Headers: map[string]string{
 &#34;X-App&#34;: &#34;web-client&#34;,
 },
 AccessToken: &#34;token-12345&#34;,
 Timeout: 2 * time.Second,
}
res := httpx.Do[map[string]any](ctx, client, req)
if res.Err != nil {
 fmt.Println(&#34;Error:&#34;, res.Err.Message)
}
</code></pre>
<p>⚙️ Performance Notes</p>
<ul>
<li>Avoid unnecessary string conversions ([]byte kept for JSON decode).</li>
<li>Timeout is per request (context-based, safe and leak-free).</li>
<li>Internally uses Resty’s pooled transport and connection reuse.</li>
<li>Designed for microservices and API-gateway-style backends.</li>
</ul>
